# CHIME CIRCUIT: flight, as in the chime-ship games. Gravity pulls the ship
# down; holding A thrusts it up (no fuel); left and right steer with
# inertia, so the ship drifts on when you let go; it faces the way it last
# steered. Thrust held with a steer helps it pick up speed that way.
# Speeds are in 1/256 px a frame: gravity 20, thrust 50, steering 16 (24
# with thrust), a drift that slows by 3 a frame, 560 at most across.
seed 1
game chime
wait 30
cheat race 1
cheat park_cpus
cheat go
cheat place 0 140 22
wait 10
expect vy0 == 200
expect y0 > 22
hold A 10
expect vy0 == -100
wait 1
expect vy0 == -80
# steering, then letting go: it drifts on
hold RIGHT 10
expect vx0 == 160
expect face0 == 1
wait 10
expect vx0 == 130
expect x0 > 142
hold LEFT 1
expect face0 == -1
expect vx0 == 114
# thrust and a steer together: the steer bites harder (24 a frame)
cheat place 0 60 40
cheat vel 0 0 0
hold RIGHT+A 10
expect vx0 == 240
expect vy0 == -300
expect face0 == 1
cheat place 0 200 40
cheat vel 0 0 0
hold LEFT+A 5
expect vx0 == -120
# the top speed across
cheat place 0 60 24
cheat vel 0 0 -300
hold RIGHT 40
expect vx0 == 560
# held thrust climbs no faster than 512
cheat place 0 140 40
cheat vel 0 0 0
hold A 20
expect vy0 == -512
# and a fall tops out at 704
cheat place 0 30 60
cheat vel 0 0 0
wait 40
expect vy0 == 704
expect walls0 == 0
